course: dictionary
lesson: 13528
title: Impersonate: copying or pretending
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: To impersonate someone means to copy their voice, look or way of moving, or to pretend to be them. Often it is for fun, to make people laugh.
explain: «Sam impersonated our teacher, Mrs Patel, and the whole class giggled.» Sam copied her voice and the way she stands, so everyone knew who it was. Impersonate is a verb, so it changes: impersonates, impersonated, impersonating.
explain: Sometimes impersonating is not a joke. «The scammer impersonated my bank and asked for my password.» The scammer pretended to be the bank to trick me. Clue words like trick and pretend show that someone is being dishonest. Before you trust a message, check who really sent it.
fact: Impersonate means to copy someone's voice, look or way of moving, or to pretend to be them.
fact: Comedians and children often impersonate famous people or teachers to make others laugh.
fact: Impersonate can also mean pretending to be someone else to trick people.
fact: Impersonating a police officer can be a crime.
fact: Impersonate is a verb: I impersonate, she impersonates, they impersonated, he is impersonating.
exercise: «Mia impersonated her big brother, copying his deep voice to make us laugh.» What does impersonated mean here? | *Copied someone's voice to make people laugh | Sang a song loudly | Shouted at someone angrily | Lost her voice completely
exercise: «The comedian impersonated the Prime Minister on stage.» Which meaning fits best? | Asked for a new job | Gave a speech about the country | Ran away from the stage | *Copied the way the person looks and talks
exercise: Find and copy the verb in this sentence: «Dad impersonates a robot when he wants to make us giggle.» | *impersonates | wants | giggle | robot
test: «The message said it was from my bank, but a scammer was impersonating the bank.» What does impersonating mean here? | Thanking people for their help | *Pretending to be someone else to trick people | Writing a long letter | Checking the money in an account
test: Why should you check before trusting a message? | Checking takes too long, so never do it | *Someone may impersonate a bank, a friend or a company to trick you | Messages are always from the people they say they are from | Friends never send messages
exam: Which sentence uses impersonate to mean pretending to trick people? | The bus was late this morning because of the rain. | We went to the park and played football. | *The fraudster impersonated a police officer to get my bank details. | The cat tried to impersonate a bird in the garden.
